I hope we don't often discuss what to radically change in Lojban, at least =
before we discuss whether Lojban needs any radical changes.=A0 That involve=
s going back to a specification of what a logical language is and seeing in=
 what ways Lojban falls short (or overachieves).=A0 In a paper I was writin=
g for LCC5 (but dropped) I worked with the minimal definition: a monparse l=
anguage in which the parse of any discourse revealed its logical structure,=
 and looked at what could be added back to the logical structure derived fr=
om a discourse that would keep the structure but be "sufficiently languagey=
".=A0 Given that definition and approach, Lojban needs no radical change, a=
nd few minor tinkerings (vocabulary excepted).=A0 What definitions and appr=
oaches suggest the need for something more radical?




